{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518011-power-to-know-all-languages","id":1518011,"title":"Power to know all languages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-15T01:01:37-07:00","id":1518011,"title":"Power to know all languages","content":"Hello everyone!<br /> <br /> I'd like some advice. I'm trying to write a 6 dots Serpentis power for Dark Ages called &quot;Wisdom of the Serpent&quot; which basically lets the character know all languages, tapping into varied symbolism like the Serpent of Eden being a temptator from before the time of the fall of Babel's Tower and the division of languages, Set being a god of foreigners, two snakes being on Mercury's staff whilst Mercury is god of communication etc.<br /> I am wondering whether it's OP for 6 dots and whether werewolves, mages or others have a similar power and at how many dots. Also, I wonder if I need to add a notice excluding some specifically supernatural and secret languages and how to phrase that best to avoid confusion between what's included and what not.<br /> <br /> The origin of the power is that I'm drawing inspiration from Aspect of the God (Guide to the Low Clans), which gives you five forms with different functions, one being the ability to intuitively understand the language of the area where you are and pass for a local, but instead of 1 power granting 5 forms, I want a few powers granting an improved version of each of those 5. In this case the improvement is that I don't simply know the local language: I understand all languages, written and spoken, and I have -1 diff from all social rolls (cumulative with the same bonus given by Serpentis 1 in Dark Ages 20) on account of intuitive understanding of customs, body language and any other aspect of communication that is not simple language.<br /> The power is free to activate (like Serpentis 1) and can be always active, as I find it weird to know languages at one moment but not at another: what if I'm thinking about a poem in Akkadian and suddenly don't know what it means anymore? It just gets weird.<br /> If needed for balance and flavour, I thought of giving it the side effect that, despite your linguistic and social proficiency, once you learn this power, people subconsciously perceive you always as a foreigner, even if you're in your homeland or live somewhere for years, unless you're actively trying to pass for a local (like with a Performance roll and / or Mask of a Thousand Faces).<br /> <br /> Is this too much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T01:26:43-07:00","id":1518012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518011-power-to-know-all-languages#post1518011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am wondering whether it's OP for 6 dots and whether werewolves, mages or others have a similar power and at how many dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes<br /> <br /> Auspex lvl. 6 power, called <b>Cipher</b>: Gain the ability to read any non-supernatural language or code<br /> It is from Archons &amp; Templars Pg. 144\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T01:29:39-07:00","id":1518013,"title":"","content":"Oka, afraid to edit<br /> Dark Thaumaturgy's Path of the Unspoken have one too<br /> <b>Scribing the Unknown</b>: Transcribe any written information\u200b<br /> and in a sense Necromancy's <b>Lifeless Tongues </b>( allows you to speak with the dead in any language)\u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T02:37:41-07:00","id":1518017,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a>thank you! I looked up the powers and they are much weaker than the one I wrote, so the one I wrote is definitely overpowered. Maybe knowledge of all languages, including supernatural ones at that point, it's a good effect for the Serpentis 9 power in VDA20 (can't remember the name) which lets you add 9 dots of attributes to your own and have a superpower agreed with the storyteller. The language and customs thing could be part of the power of an intellectual or socially oriented form.<br /> Alternatively, as a 6 dots power, the vampire may need to spend 1 blood point and roll Intelligence + Occult (or Theology) to temporarily be able to understand and communicate in any human non-specialised language he comes across, written or spoken, without deciphering codes though. He could, for example, read a tablet on medicine from ancient Babylon in Akkadian, but he would understand it as a native babylonian would have, not as a physician, as for that he would require dots in Medicine. He would grasp idiomatic expressions but not terminology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T03:40:46-07:00","id":1518019,"title":"","content":"You could adjust the power by making it more conditional; I recently made a <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits?p=1515316#post1515316\">Path</a> with a Level 3 power that allows to pick up new Abilities (including languages) through immersion that still requires XP, but reduces the cost.<br /> <br /> For example, your Serpentis power could require another person present who has knowledge of the language and whose mind you borrow with the Discipline to use them as a proxy for 'understanding'. That would still allow easy conversation and reading/writing in an extant language, but for dead languages you would need someone who knows them. It also limits the scope to the vocabulary and literacy of the proxy - if they don't know a word, you don't either. And it provides a good reason why you would lose the understanding of the language once the power runs out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T05:36:17-07:00","id":1518025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1518011-power-to-know-all-languages?p=1518019#post1518019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, your Serpentis power could require another person present who has knowledge of the language and whose mind you borrow with the Discipline to use them as a proxy for 'understanding'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Similar Mytherceria powers exist<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022 <b>Steal the Mind</b><br /> Legends tell of the Fair Folk taking the memories and faculties of their victims, leaving these hapless people drooling idiots for the rest of their lives. While modern thinking is that these stories actually referred to stroke victims, elder Kiasyd display a power with a similar effect.<br /> The victim of Steal the Mind loses his memories and all knowledge he has accumulated. The Kiasyd gains these memories for a short time, and generally uses this time to inscribe them before they revert to the original owner\u2026 assuming the Weirdling lets that happen.<br /> <b>System: </b>The player selects a mortal or supernatural target and rolls Perception + Subterfuge (difficulty equal to the target\u2019s current Willpower). While the Kiasyd has \u201cstolen\u201d her subject\u2019s mind, she retains her own consciousness, but has complete access to all of the subject\u2019s thoughts and memories.<br /> Subjects have no knowledge that they have been affected in this manner, though any attempts to harm them \u2014 by the Kiasyd or anyone else \u2014 return their wits to them immediately.<br /> Subjects have no access to their Knowledges while this power is active, but Talents and most Skills (those that work on muscle memory) are still present.<br /> The Storyteller might need to exercise discretion as to which Abilities are lost.<br /> Those who are victims of this power for long periods of time may starve, though they will eat food presented to them.<br /> The number of successes determines the duration of the effect, though the Kiasyd may return the subject\u2019s mind at any time before this period ends. If the victim dies before the memories return, the Weirdling keeps them.<br /> If the Kiasyd kills the target to keep his memory, the character may need to roll for degeneration depending on what Path they follow \u2014 Kiasyd on Humanity must always roll.<br /> 1 Success - 10 minutes<br /> 2 Successes - One hour<br /> 3 Successes - One night<br /> 4 Successes - One week<br /> 5 Successes - One month<br /> <br /> Interestingly this is quite strangly worded one; &quot;The player selects a mortal or supernatural target&quot; no touch, nothing, you don't have to see as per RAW... just... select someone you know?<br /> It was always murky at best, personally tend to a bit house rule it, you have actually see your target to use it (or enter its mind vie Auspex)<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022 <b>Absorb the Mind</b><br /> This power, similar to Steal the Mind, allows the vampire to absorb Abilities from her victim.<br /> These traits are transferred <i>permanently;</i> the victim loses the knowledge, and the Kindred gains it.<br /> Absorb the Mind is an extremely invasive and insidious power, and fortunately only a bare handful of Kindred in the world know of it.<br /> <b>System:</b> The player rolls Perception + Empathy (difficulty equal to the target\u2019s current Willpower). The target may resist with a Willpower roll (difficulty equal to the Kiasyd\u2019s current Willpower). The difference between the two determines the effect. If the target gets more successes, he resists completely and the Kiasyd<i> may never use Absorb the Mind on this target again</i>!<br /> The Kiasyd, if successful, may select a combination of Abilities to her satisfaction.<br /> Taking some of a victim\u2019s Ability dots may leave a remainder \u2014 the Kiasyd need not take all of a subject\u2019s dots in a given Ability.<br /> For example, a character with three dots in Occult, from whom a Kiasyd steals one, retains an Occult of 2. If a Kiasyd takes fewer dots than she already has in a given Ability, these points do not serve to raise her own rating. (In the previous example, the Kiasyd would not increase his Occult rating if he already had a rating of one or more, as he took only one dot.)<br /> If the Kiasyd fails in an attempt to use this power on a target, no subsequent attempt can be made on that target for a year and a day.<br /> In all cases, the maximum to which the Kiasyd can raise an Ability is the level the target has in that Ability, so if a victim has only one dot in Law and the Kiasyd gets 2 successes, she can\u2019t gain 2 dots in Law.<br /> Generational restrictions do apply: a Sixth-Generation Kiasyd can have a maximum of seven dots in an Ability, for example. All losses of Abilities on the part of the victim are permanent, though they may be returned to their original levels via experience-point expenditure.<br /> 1 Success - Steal 1 dot<br /> 2 Successes - Steal 2 dots in one Ability<br /> 3 Successes - Steal 3 dots in up to two Abilities<br /> 4 Successes - Steal 4 dots in up to three Abilities<br /> 5 Successes - Steal 5 dots in up to four Abilities<br /> <br /> At least with the levle 7 power, the victim may resist...<br /> But in my humble opinions, these are quite brutal powers, and ideal to be used as a template to your Serpentis power<br /> <br /> Even combine it from a bit &quot;stolen&quot; knwoledge (or provided to them, dempending of the point of view) of the Silent Strider secret camp, Eaters of The Dead<br /> The<i> forbidden</i> rite is known <b>Rite of Dormant Wisdom</b><br /> The practitioner and his aides may gain the knowledge and memories of a dead person by ritually devouring the deceased's brain.<br /> The corpse can be long dead, as long as the brain hasn't fully decomposed.<br /> Those participating in the rite must roll Intelligence + Occult (difficulty 9).<br /> The number of successes determines how complete the memory transference is: one indicates that the Eater gains the dead one's most recent memories, while five confers total life memories. No special abilities (Disciplines, Gifts, or the like) can be learned from this rite, but the Eater may learn any number of passwords or occult knowledge.<br /> However, the Wyrm's touch is on this rite. If the rite is practiced more times than the character has Gnosis, then the character will become wholly of the Wyrm, servant of Foebok, Urge Wyrm of Fear.<br /> A botch will also destroy the character's mind, making him an insane slave to the Wyrm. If the ritemaster and his aides each spend a permanent Gnosis point, they may perform this rite on a Garou or mummy. The rite also works on immobilized or torporous vampires, although cutting into a Leech's cranium will certainly awaken it.<br /> <br /> Serpentis or Akhu ritual coul\u00e9d be mimic this<br /> Prepare your victim ritually and eat her brain... or haert, since the Ancient Egyptians believed that the heart, rather than the brain, was the source of human wisdom, as well as emotions, memory, the soul and the personality itself!<br /> <br /> Since Serpentis already have a quasi-ritualistic power, <b>Cheat the Scale of Anubis </b>and<b>The Heart of Darkness </b>to remove the heart and an instant version of it, the level 8 <b>Heart Thief</b> it is easy to desing some ritual, or even power to rip out and devour the heart how Apep devours the Light to stole memories and knowledge<br /> Or an Akhu ritual/serpentis power that targets the Heart in the victim to &quot;stole&quot; the knowledge from it like the Mytherceria powers above \u200b<br /> <br /> <b>The opening of the mouth </b>ceremony (or ritual) was an ancient Egyptian ritual described in funerary texts such as the Pyramid Texts. From the Old Kingdom to the Roman Period, there is ample evidence of this ceremony, which was believed to give the deceased their fundamental senses to carry out tasks in the afterlife. - this served to restore the senses of the newly deceased (resident in spirit within the mummified body or a statue), so that he or she could once again breathe, speak, eat, drink, see, and hear.<br /> So maybe mimicking it, your ability or ritual &quot;opens your mouth&quot; and make you able to &quot;speak&quot; - eg. use language of any kind\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T05:48:27-07:00","id":1518026,"title":"","content":"Sorry, today my min a bit absent, and forgot thing - but afraid to edit<br /> In Gehenna Set after his return simply tore out someones tounge and ate it, fused it with his own and was able to speak and udnerstand the language(s) of the modern age<br /> This is a nice idea to used too as an inspriation to your power; eat the tounge and gain the knowledge for a limited time - or permanently, dealer's choice<br /> Or a nice &quot;fetish&quot;/artifact, a mumified tounge of a professor of linguistics... and your settite carry around and use its power (or the Wraith shackled to his own tounge), as a &quot;translator&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T17:49:04-07:00","id":1518115,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> I really like the idea of an Akhu ritual to consume someone's heart or organs to increase one's traits and gain knowledge. In VDA20 the removal of the heart has become a level 5 Akhu ritual rather than a Serpentis power. A level 6+ ritual would be perfect for the ability theft power. That edition has already enough powers (Mytherceria, Protean's Loki's Gift, the Path of Skulls of Necromancy, one of Abombwe's powers...) to steal traits to make it perfectly viable","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}